    "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A3.SS1",
    "original_text": "Attributed ASTIS-authored analytic integration for fixed PBPS C.1, not a printed standalone theorem.\nLet E be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert space with its Borel measurable structure, including rank zero. Let V:E→ℝ be C2, α>0, and D²V(x)[v,v]≥α‖v‖² for all x,v. Let η>0 and let f:E→ℝ be C1 with compact support. Define μ=volume.tilted(−V), R_y=μ.tilted(x↦−‖x−y‖²/(2η)), and the literal source law S_y=volume.tilted(u↦−V((y+u)/2)−‖y−u‖²/(8η)). Then for EVERY y, S_y=(x↦2x−y)_#R_y, and the exact mean function y↦∫f(u)S_y(du) is C1. All actual Gibbs normalization, integrability, affine law and mean regularity ingredients are produced internally. This is attributed analytic integration for PBPS C.1, with explicitly broader sufficient background assumptions, not a standalone printed main theorem or rough B.13.\nSource boundary: ASTIS-authored analytic integration for pinned PBPS2609.06905v1 C.1 actual reflected density A3.Ex1 physical4581-4587, A3.Ex2 4589-4595 and normalized-density differentiation A3.E1 4597-4604; smooth compact core4573-4576 and C.2 physical4654-4664 toward B.13 physical3779-3786. This is not printed standalone theorem.\nExplicit extension: Explicit sufficient-background generalization: finite real Hilbert/Borel E including rank0, C2 V with positive global lower Hessian, eta>0, signed compact C1 f. Original paper also has upper Hessian beta and beta*eta<=1 and smooth compact f. Upper bound and step cap are not needed for this analytic edge; genuine paper consumer retains them. This is attributed background extension, never replacement of B.13 assumptions.\nActual objects: At EVERY y: mu=volume.tilted(-V), R_y=mu.tilted(-norm(x-y)^2/(2eta)), literal SOURCE S_y=volume.tilted(-V((y+u)/2)-norm(y-u)^2/(8eta)). Simultaneously prove actual S_y=(2x-y)#R_y and literal S_y compact mean C1. No arbitrary AE conditional version.\nFuture consumer: Real50 source-density Tf compact C1, then actual51 outer Gaussian gradient closure using actual50 Lp representatives and WeightedC1GradientDomain.c1_in_closed_gradient. Both pointwise source-law and mean regularity are needed; no closure consumer completed before it is proved.",
    "text_sha256": "63326d943bf0d3d2a4b3e3895c65e92bc515c394363cc752596373bbd5db5832"
  },
  "lean": {
    "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.ProximalBPS.LiteralReflectedMean.reflected_gibbs_mean_c1",
    "file": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/ProximalBPS/LiteralReflectedMean.lean",
    "statement": "\n    {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]\n    [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]\n    {V : E → ℝ} {α η : ℝ} (hα : 0 < α) (hV : ContDiff ℝ 2 V)\n    (hH : ∀ x v : E, α*‖v‖^2 ≤ (fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v) v)\n    (hη : 0 < η) {f : E → ℝ} (hf : ContDiff ℝ 1 f) (hc : HasCompactSupport f) :\n    let μ := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x => -V x)\n    let R := fun y : E => μ.tilted (fun x => -‖x-y‖^2/(2*η))\n    let S := fun y : E => (volume : Measure E).tilted\n      (fun u => -V ((1/2:ℝ) • (y+u)) - ‖y-u‖^2/(8*η))\n    (∀ y, S y = (R y).map (fun x : E => (2:ℝ) • x-y)) ∧\n      ContDiff ℝ 1 (fun y : E => ∫ u, f u ∂S y)",
    "statement_sha256": "2ffa67092cac8a25fb4c9aef6cb402b54329b2f9e3d305161a46a6f3e599a6dc",
    "compiled": true,
    "formalizer": "root-samplinglib-writer",
    "decoder_context": [
      "E is a finite-dimensional real inner-product space with canonical Lebesgue/Haar volume and Borel measurable structure, including rank zero. V is globally C2, alpha>0 is a genuine lower Hessian bound and eta>0. The observer f is globally C1 with compact support and can have either sign.",
      "fderiv real (fderiv real V) x v applied to v is the actual directional bilinear Hessian under global C2; its lower bound alpha*norm(v)^2 is explicit. No upper Hessian or upper step restriction appears in this exact analytic statement.",
      "Measure.tilted means actual normalized exponential tilt: mu.tilted(q) has density exp(q)/integral exp(q) dmu when its exponential weight is integrable. Canonical volume is the literal reference measure, never an arbitrary caller density. Probability, partition positivity/finiteness and L1 are not supplied premises.",
      "mu is literally volume.tilted(-V). R(y) is literally its quadratic likelihood tilt -norm(x-y)^2/(2eta). S(y) is literally the displayed volume tilt -V(half*(y+u))-norm(y-u)^2/(8eta), specified at every parameter y. No arbitrary AE conditional version is selected.",
      "Measure.map is the actual measurable pushforward. The map x->2x-y has inverse u->half*(u+y); scale and translation are actual vector operations, not transport certificates. The integral is real Bochner expectation of the arbitrary observer under the exact displayed measure.",
      "ContDiff real1 means global C1 of the exact whole mean function, with genuine continuous Frechet derivative. HasCompactSupport refers to compact closure of its nonzero support. The statement includes no caller law-equality, derivative-continuity, integrability, normalizer or closed-gradient certificate.",
      "No transition trajectory, rough-observer domain, convergence/mixing, numerical error, oracle cost or algorithm complexity claim is supplied by these predicates."
    ],
    "compiler_evidence": "runs/20261007-companion-priority/pbps-literal-reflected-mean53/tests.1.log PASS3895: original PBPS SAME mu/J Markov conditional, every source S reflection/probability, rank0 SOURCE-volume mean1 derivative0; three standard3 closures."
  },
