          "text": "The genuine Tests use the original two-sided Hessian and βη≤1 assumptions. MacroscopicEnergy supplies probability of the same μ; GaussianConditionalKernel constructs a Markov conditional R for the same Gaussian augmentation J and identifies every literal posterior fiber. The new law identity yields every source S_y probability and its smooth compact mean C1. Separately, dimension0 with V=0, α=η=1 and f=1 produces actual source mean1 and actual derivative0. Neither Test assumes centering or a closure certificate.",
          "formula": "J=\\operatorname{law}(X,X+\\sqrt\\eta G),\\quad R\\text{ is Markov and conditional for }J,\\quad S_y=(2x-y)_\\#R_y;\\qquad d=0,\\ V=0,\\ f=1:\\ m\\equiv1,\\ Dm\\equiv0.",
