      "lean_statement": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert space with its Borel measurable structure, including rank zero. Let V:E→ℝ be C2, α>0, and D²V(x)[v,v]≥α‖v‖² for all x,v. Let η>0 and let f:E→ℝ be C1 with compact support. Define μ=volume.tilted(−V), R_y=μ.tilted(x↦−‖x−y‖²/(2η)), and the literal source law S_y=volume.tilted(u↦−V((y+u)/2)−‖y−u‖²/(8η)). Then for EVERY y, S_y=(x↦2x−y)_#R_y, and the exact mean function y↦∫f(u)S_y(du) is C1. All actual Gibbs normalization, integrability, affine law and mean regularity ingredients are produced internally. This is attributed analytic integration for PBPS C.1, with explicitly broader sufficient background assumptions, not a standalone printed main theorem or rough B.13.",
      "lean_proof": "Produce genuine Gibbs normalization before using a tilt; Identify the actual posterior as the combined normalized potential; Keep the exact inverse map and the factor8η; Apply the genuine normalized affine-map theorem; Transport the whole literal mean function, then use true C1 regularity; Consume the paper’s original kernel and a noncentered rank-zero source law",
